From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] iokit: build ACPICA and NeoDarwin's ACPI platform

SBSA machines describe their devices in ACPI: the DSDT and SSDTs name the
PCI host bridge, the UART, virtio-mmio slots, the GED and the rest, with
their registers and interrupts in AML (_CRS). XNU has no AML interpreter;
on Intel Macs Apple's closed AppleACPIPlatform kext was one. P1-09 builds
ACPICA (acpica/acpica 20260408, used under its BSD-3-Clause licence;
overlaid at iokit/ndacpi/acpica) into the kernel with NeoDarwin's ACPI
platform (kernel/neodarwin/acpi, overlaid at iokit/ndacpi): ACPICA's OS
layer, the ACPI platform driver and IOACPIPlatformDevice. They are compiled
in, as the platform expert is (patch 0009), because kcgen links no kexts
until M5. NeoDarwinPlatformExpert starts the ACPI platform.

This patch lists the files for arm64: ACPICA's core (dispatcher, events,
executer, hardware, namespace, parser, resources, tables, utilities; no
debugger, disassembler or tools) and NeoDarwin's three. ACPICA's objects
are compiled with -include acnd.h, NeoDarwin's host configuration, which
stands in for the platform header ACPICA would pick for __APPLE__, so
ACPICA itself is not patched.

Rebase-risk: low (appended entries; applies after 0009).
